{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/390846-going-native-questions","id":390846,"title":"Going Native questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-02T19:26:57-08:00","id":390846,"title":"Going Native questions","content":"Going Native is the ultimate disguise for a Demon, useful for those times when 10 dots of Cover isn't enough... but it's so effective that it shuts down almost all of a Demon's special abilities. Three questions:<br /> <br /> First, a Demon using Going Native is hit by a Knight of St. Adrian using Fist of Revelation or Bear Mace. What wins out, the Ink or the Embed?<br /> <br /> Second, is a Demon using this embed capable of triggering a Compromise during use? The embed vaguely implies that it triggers a Compromise when the Embed ends, but during use, the Demon effectively stops being a Demon with a Cover, and becomes a vanilla human. Avoiding Compromise seems like an appropriate extension of this effect.<br /> <br /> Third, does Going Native shut down other embeds activated earlier in the scene? I'm thinking of Alibi, Occam's Razor, and Persistent Legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 02-02-2015, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T19:49:08-08:00","id":390869,"title":"","content":"Bear Mace isn't keyed to demonic nature, but as you're mortal that's irrelevant. In this case, I'd say the Embed, because it really is effectively severing off the things that make you supernatural. You literally are just your cover.<br /> <br /> I don't imagine you can Compromise while human. This is more based off of a hunch than my understanding of the game's metaphysics(Because it seems to be one part observer effect, one part burning of reality, and one part clash of identities), but I'd run with that.<br /> <br /> I'd say, mostly, yes, if it's directly affecting you, as in you the person, not others. In your three examples, Persistent Legend would die, Occam's razor is technically already done and over with so it would still be in effect from when you ran the reality aspect, and Alibi can run off of your severed identity/infinity engine without relying on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:09:14-08:00","id":391234,"title":"","content":"My opinion - For all intents and purposes, when you've Gone Native, you are 100 percent mortal. You pretend, for the duration, you never had a demon template, and only a core mortal one. So, the &quot;Ink&quot; should fail, imho. The whole point of the embed is to be mortal, so let the rules reflect that you are a mortal. Its the embeds raison d'etre.<br /> <br /> If you really feel like there needs to be some debate? Clash of Wills is EXACTLY the the rule for this kind of situation. Alternatively, ask yourself which is more thematic for the group you are playing with. If a demon game, then its lame and frankly renders the power pointless if the Ink can auto win. If a Hunter game, its lame if a demon can avoid detection this way. If its a mixed group, I'm not going to comment, as a demon and an angel-blessed demon hunter together is kind of far out of my comfort zone.<br /> <br /> No, I don't think you can compromise while a mortal. Mortals can't compromise.<br /> <br /> Yes, it would &quot;shut down&quot; other active embeds. Vanilla mortals can't do those kinds of things. As well, I would argue it would shut down any ability to activate Legend, your ability to lie freely, or the mental tricks to avoid having your mind read. You lose any and all benefits of being a supernatural being. You are fully, utterly, completely and entirely a rank mortal. At best, you have the equivalent of Unseen Sense (God Machine) in terms of supernatural ability, and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}